<article class="env-definition" id="02RB">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02RB">Definition <span data-tag="02RB">42.14.1</span>.</a> Let $(S, \delta )$ be as in Situation <a href="/tag/02QL" data-tag="02QL">42.7.1</a>. Let $X$, $Y$ be locally of finite type over $S$. Let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism. Assume $f$ is flat of relative dimension $r$. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
Let $Z \subset Y$ be an integral closed subscheme of $\delta $-dimension $k$. We define $f^*[Z]$ to be the $(k+r)$-cycle on $X$ to the scheme theoretic inverse image 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  f^*[Z] = [f^{-1}(Z)]_{k+r}.  \]
</div>
<p>
 This makes sense since $\dim _\delta (f^{-1}(Z)) = k + r$ by Lemma <a href="/tag/02R8" data-tag="02R8">42.13.1</a>. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
Let $\alpha = \sum n_ i [Z_ i]$ be a $k$-cycle on $Y$. The <em>flat pullback of $\alpha $ by $f$</em> is the sum 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  f^* \alpha = \sum n_ i f^*[Z_ i]  \]
</div>
<p>
 where each $f^*[Z_ i]$ is defined as above. The sum is locally finite by Lemma <a href="/tag/02R9" data-tag="02R9">42.13.2</a>. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
We denote $f^* : Z_ k(Y) \to Z_{k + r}(X)$ the map of abelian groups so obtained. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>